            <ArticleTitle>The effects of obesity on pulmonary function in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000522135.76069.ce</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prevalence of obesity has risen rapidly in the United States in the past 20 years. Up to 25% of US children are obese, and obesity can be directly correlated with immediate and long-term health consequences. Pediatric obesity can harm multiple body systems and is a public health issue. This article focuses on how obesity affects a child's respiratory system, including pulmonary function, exercise intolerance, gas exchange, and airway musculature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
